<a name="id08100090110004"></a> 
<p class="servinfosub-title"> <span class="servinfosub-head"></span>Component Procedure</p> 
<dl> 
 <dd> 
  <div class="attention1-label">
    Warning 
  </div> 
 </dd> 
 <dd> 
  <div class="attention1"> 
   <div class="list">
     • Handling the sophisticated airbag sensor control module (SAS_CM) improperly can accidentally operate (deploy) the air bag module and pre-tensioner seat belt, which may seriously injure you. Read the air bag system service warnings and cautions before handling the sophisticated airbag sensor control module (SAS_CM). (See 
    <font class="extxref-label"><a href="index?page=content&amp;id=SM3868811">AIR BAG SYSTEM SERVICE WARNINGS</a></font>.) (See 
    <font class="extxref-label"><a href="index?page=content&amp;id=SM3868812">AIR BAG SYSTEM SERVICE CAUTIONS</a></font>.) 
   </div> 
   <div class="list">
     • If the connector is connected and the main power is switched ON (ENG RUN/ENG OFF) with the sophisticated airbag sensor control module (SAS_CM) not secured completely using the installation nuts, the sophisticated airbag sensor control module (SAS_CM) may detect a degree of impact even when something contacts it lightly, deploying the air bag module and pre-tensioner seat belt accidentally. 
   </div> 
   <div class="list">
     • If [Calibrating DSC related Sensor] is not completed, the DSC will not operate normally which could lead to an unexpected accident. Therefore, if the electronically controlled brake unit (EBU) or the sophisticated airbag sensor control module (SAS_CM) is replaced or removed/installed, be sure to perform [Calibrating DSC related Sensor] so that the DSC will operate normally. 
   </div> 
  </div> 
 </dd> 
</dl> 
